<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Husaby</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Husaby is a village and early church site in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vastergotland">Västergötland</a>, south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>, near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-vanern">Lake Vänern</a>. Tradition holds that King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olof-skotkonung">Olof Skötkonung</a> was baptised at a spring there in the early 11th century by the English missionary Sigfrid, and Husaby is regarded as one of the cradles of the Swedish church. Its 12th-century stone church, with a massive western tower, is among the oldest in Sweden.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/husaby.jpg" alt="Husaby" width="320" height="286" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 1.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Husaby_kyrka_ext_2005-08-10.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
